  "body": "## Goal\n\nImprove remaining keyboard/accessibility polish from the PR 14 screenshot follow-up without blocking the data-correctness PR.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Custom days input should include a stable `name`, `autocomplete`, `inputmode`, and clearer placeholder copy such as `e.g. 14`.\n- Chart canvas should have an accessible name and fallback text / data summary for non-visual users.\n- Loading copy should use the typographic ellipsis `Loading…` consistently.\n- Focused source/model state should be visible through more than border color alone.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Keyboard and screen-reader users can understand the custom range input and chart purpose.\n- Chart has an accessible label or fallback description tied to the visible chart title/summary.\n- Loading text is consistent across the template.\n- Active/focused state uses text/icon/background treatment in addition to color/border.\n\n## Notes\n\nPR 14 already keeps source-card filtering on the source name button and moves long source/path metadata into the info affordance. Keep this issue scoped to the remaining accessibility/input polish.",
